From a605f5748fb0dbc8f0990be2c77adb263589b85e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 04:34:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Cancel budgeted exact work cooperatively

Closure-plan M4 needs cooperative cancellation that publishes no partial
result, releases temporary state and does not poison a retry. Work-budget
scopes had none, and the stalled bevel stroke of a filleted hyperbola pair
spends minutes in loops that charge no work units.

CancellationToken, with_cancellable_budget and WorkBudget::UNLIMITED add a
thread-safe request to the shared scope stack. The next admitted unit or
exhaustion check reports WorkKind::Cancellation and the scope publishes no
value; outer tokens stop nested scopes, nested tokens leave parents running.
Integer polynomial Bareiss determinants, pseudo-quotient multiplication
matrices and dense tensor products observe exhaustion between steps and
return their existing unavailable outcome. Hypercurve adds
evaluate_with_cancellable_budget.

The stalled stroke now returns Cancellation within 0.16-0.45 s of a request;
before, a request after 60 s was not honored in 21 minutes. Warm cancelled
attempts retain at most a few KB of a 4.7 MB peak. WorkKind gains a variant;
docs/MIGRATIONS.md records the caller action.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
